# Summary
This commit introduced the retry loop and its budget-checking bug. The previous code sent a heartbeat request once and therefore did not have this specific post-deadline retry behavior.
The commit adds bounded retry for Unix control-plane heartbeat refreshes, using the requested lease duration as the retry budget. However, after a retryable transport error, the loop checks that the current time is before the deadline, sleeps for min(remaining, backoff), and then immediately starts the next loop iteration. If the remaining time is less than or equal to the backoff, this sleeps until the deadline and then sends another request at or after the deadline. Repeated immediate failures can also lead to a final attempt starting at the lease boundary. That undermines the intended cap and can allow a stale heartbeat retry to be applied after the requested lease window. A robust implementation should recheck the deadline before each send attempt and avoid sleeping all the way to the deadline when another request will be sent afterward.

# Resolution
Fixed in e3b298c87cb6696c2afc8a9dcf6dd347238909cb (`Bound heartbeat retry by lease budget`).

The fix makes `UnixControlPlaneClient::send_liveness_request` re-check the lease-derived retry deadline before every heartbeat retry send. If the deadline has been reached, it returns the last retryable transport error instead of sending a stale heartbeat. Heartbeat retries now use a short liveness-specific backoff so lost-response recovery can still happen inside the lease window without sleeping all the way to the deadline.

The regression test `unix_control_plane_client_does_not_send_heartbeat_retry_at_lease_deadline` exercises the real `UnixControlPlaneClient::refresh_node_heartbeat` Unix socket path. It starts with the socket absent, binds the listener only after the 50 ms retry budget has expired, and asserts that no retry connection is accepted after that deadline. Adjacent lost-response heartbeat retry tests were also run to confirm valid in-window retries still work.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm the heartbeat liveness retry loop has no deadline recheck immediately before each send attempt.
- [x] Confirm the retry budget is exactly the requested heartbeat lease duration.
- [x] Exercise the actual UnixControlPlaneClient::refresh_node_heartbeat path, not a standalone model.
- [x] Force a retryable transport error before the budget expires and make the server available before the budget deadline.
- [x] Demonstrate the next heartbeat request is accepted at/after the requested budget and applied by the authority, extending the lease.
## Report
Validated the finding with a targeted Rust unit-test PoC. Code review confirmed the vulnerable path: crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:4006-4017 computes deadline once, checks Instant::now() < deadline only after a failed send, sleeps remaining.min(100ms), and then loops directly back to self.send_request without a pre-send deadline check. crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:4441-4448 derives retry_budget from heartbeat.requested_lease_duration_ms for RefreshNodeHeartbeat. I added a focused PoC test that starts refresh_node_heartbeat while the Unix socket is absent, causing a retryable NotFound transport error; a real Unix listener appears 10ms later, before the 50ms requested lease/retry budget expires. The vulnerable loop sleeps to the deadline and then sends the heartbeat anyway. The server accepted it at ~51-53ms and applied it at modeled authority time 2060ms, extending the lease deadline to Some(2110). The test intentionally asserts the intended invariant that the retry must be accepted before the 50ms budget; it panics on the vulnerable commit. Command output: `BUG: heartbeat retry was accepted at 51.816475ms, at/after the requested 50ms budget, and the authority applied a fresh lease deadline Some(2110)`. I also checked memory/debugger tooling: valgrind and gdb were not installed; lldb was available and running the test under lldb reproduced the same failing assertion, though the process exited before a stopped backtrace could be collected.

# Evidence
crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs (L4006 to 4017)
  Note: The deadline is checked only before sleeping; after sleeping up to the remaining budget, the loop retries without rechecking whether the deadline has already been reached.
```
        let deadline = Instant::now() + retry_budget;
        loop {
            match self.send_request(kind, payload) {
                Ok(payload) => return Ok(payload),
                Err(error)
                    if error.is_retryable_control_plane_rpc_transport_error()
                        && Instant::now() < deadline =>
                {
                    let now = Instant::now();
                    let remaining = deadline.saturating_duration_since(now);
                    std::thread::sleep(remaining.min(CONTROL_PLANE_RPC_CHECK_APPLIED_BACKOFF));
                }
```

crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs (L4441 to 4448)
  Note: The retry budget is derived from the heartbeat's requested lease duration, so retrying after this budget violates the intended lease-bound behavior.
```
        let mut payload = Vec::new();
        write_node_heartbeat(&mut payload, &heartbeat)?;
        let retry_budget = Duration::from_millis(heartbeat.requested_lease_duration_ms);
        let payload = self.send_liveness_request(
            ControlPlaneRpcKind::RefreshNodeHeartbeat,
            &payload,
